BO_ 1411 MS_583_NodeStartup: 1 Vector__XXX
 SG_ MS_583_NodeStartup_Data : 7|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX

CM_ "Logs: truck = friend 2011 bus (VIN in 0x40A, full node set); bench = isolated module(s) on Bo bench, origin unknown (no VIN, only node 03 or 03+27 on the ring). MS-CAN 125 kbit/s (high confidence: back-to-back 8-byte frames are ~1.0 ms apart = ~125 bits at 125k). Recorded 2020-06-02 on a friend 2011 F-350 KR 4x4 (log header + VIN 1FT8W3BT4BE****** in 0x40A, same truck as the HS drive log), plus a bench HVAC+DCSM log 2020-06-12 (no VIN; module origin unknown). Assumed to match Bo 2012 Lariat parts (unverified). The 2020 logs have many single-bit-corrupted frames and stray FD/RTR/extended IDs, so one-off IDs were ignored.";
CM_ BO_ 928 "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:18 KOES (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus, captures/2020-mscan src22GEX); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan)] Bo (forum 2020): sending 45 00 80 02 89 24 00 00 every 200 ms enables the HVAC controls without 0x501. In the truck it is sent every 1000 ms (also in the 19:18 KOES log, b0=0x45). 2020-06-04 bench replay run 2: the module woke (503) before 3A0 was sent, so 3A0 is the controls-enable, not the NM wake (inferred). 2020-06-10 bench, 3A0 alone at 200 ms: HVAC node stays awake for the whole 19 s in LimpHome (503 03 04 at 1 Hz, never SleepInd) and seat-climate presses show in 0x124. 2020-06-12 bench (HVAC+DCSM, no 0x501): ring 03<->27 stays up while 3A0 runs; ~5.4 s after the last 3A0 both send SleepInd+SleepAck and go quiet. So 3A0 acts as the application keep-awake (likely the power-mode/ignition message), medium. Forum 2020 wake set (3E2, 40A, 423, 425, 426, 42C, 10D, 3A0, 3B2, 3B3) = frames 21-30 of the 19:18 KOES truck capture, i.e. one 1-s burst of periodic frames (selected by replaying the first 10/20/30/40/50 frames, inferred). Replayed alone on 2020-06-04 it woke the bench module.";
CM_ SG_ 928 PowerModeCandidate "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:18 KOES (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus, captures/2020-mscan src22GEX); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan)] b0: 0x11 in the key-off log, 0x11/0x15/0x44/0x45 in the KOES log. On the bench, 3A0 with b0=0x45 every 200 ms holds the HVAC/DCSM awake, so this is probably ignition/power mode (0x45 = run).";
CM_ SG_ 928 Unknown_B1_5 "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:18 KOES (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus, captures/2020-mscan src22GEX); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan)] Constant 00 80 02 89 24 in both logs.";
CM_ SG_ 928 Unknown_B6_7 "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:18 KOES (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus, captures/2020-mscan src22GEX); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan)] Constant 00 00.";
CM_ BO_ 947 "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus)] Wake set frame. Forum/KOES value 00 43 05 12 00 00 00 38; key off 00 43 05 00 00 00 00 00. 1000 ms. Different layout from HS 0x3B3. Forum 2020 wake set (3E2, 40A, 423, 425, 426, 42C, 10D, 3A0, 3B2, 3B3) = frames 21-30 of the 19:18 KOES truck capture, i.e. one 1-s burst of periodic frames (selected by replaying the first 10/20/30/40/50 frames, inferred). Replayed alone on 2020-06-04 it woke the bench module.";
CM_ SG_ 947 Unknown_B0_2 "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus)] 00 43 05 typical.";
CM_ SG_ 947 Unknown_B3 "[conf=low] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus)] 0x12 with ignition on, 0x00 key off.";
CM_ SG_ 947 Unknown_B4_6 "[conf=low] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus)] Mostly 0.";
CM_ SG_ 947 Unknown_B7 "[conf=low] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus)] 0x38 or 0x30 with ignition on, 0x00 key off.";
CM_ BO_ 292 "[conf=medium] [src=MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834)] Sent by the HVAC/climate module (node 03) at ~1008 ms plus immediately on change; it was the only node on the 2020-06-04 and 06-10 benches and still sent it. Carries the climate-seat (TED heat/cool) selections, most likely the HVAC -> DCSM request Bo found in 2020 (medium). 0x125 on the truck carries the same payloads (DCSM echo/status? low).";
CM_ SG_ 292 SeatClimate_B0 "[conf=medium] [src=MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834)] b0: first seat (driver? low). One-hot climate-seat state. On the bench each press steps 80->40->20->02(off) and 10->08->04->02(off), i.e. two modes with 3 levels each. Bo (2026-10): each seat (driver and passenger) has 3 heating and 3 cooling levels, so one mode is heat and the other cool (medium), but which is which is NOT known, and which byte is driver is NOT confirmed (low); the level encoding is medium. Truck KOES log (Driver Seat, Pass Seat test) shows 10 10 and 02 02.";
CM_ SG_ 292 SeatClimate_B1 "[conf=medium] [src=MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834)] b1: second seat (passenger? low). Same encoding; seen on the 2020-06-12 bench stepping 80,10,08,04,02 while b0 stayed 10 or 02. One-hot climate-seat state. On the bench each press steps 80->40->20->02(off) and 10->08->04->02(off), i.e. two modes with 3 levels each. Bo (2026-10): each seat (driver and passenger) has 3 heating and 3 cooling levels, so one mode is heat and the other cool (medium), but which is which is NOT known, and which byte is driver is NOT confirmed (low); the level encoding is medium. Truck KOES log (Driver Seat, Pass Seat test) shows 10 10 and 02 02.";
CM_ SG_ 292 Unknown_B2_7 "[conf=medium] [src=MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834)] Always 0 apart from single-bit noise.";
CM_ BO_ 862 "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); bench 0x5xx HVAC+DCSM log 2020-06-12 (bench modules, origin unknown); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan)] HVAC-module periodic output (also sent with only node 03 on the bench). Typical 80 00 00 00 00 00 00 00. ~1008 ms. Varying bytes [0, 1, 2, 4, 5, 7], typical 80 00 00 00 00 00 00 00.";
CM_ SG_ 862 MS_35E_HVAC_Data "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); bench 0x5xx HVAC+DCSM log 2020-06-12 (bench modules, origin unknown); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan)] Undecoded payload, big-endian integer of all bytes.";
CM_ BO_ 999 "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); bench 0x5xx HVAC+DCSM log 2020-06-12 (bench modules, origin unknown); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan)] HVAC-module periodic output (also sent with only node 03 on the bench). Typical all zeros. ~1008 ms. Varying bytes [2, 3, 5, 6], typical 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00.";
CM_ SG_ 999 MS_3E7_HVAC_Data "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); bench 0x5xx HVAC+DCSM log 2020-06-12 (bench modules, origin unknown); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan)] Undecoded payload, big-endian integer of all bytes.";
CM_ BO_ 1050 "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); bench 0x5xx HVAC+DCSM log 2020-06-12 (bench modules, origin unknown); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan)] HVAC-module periodic output (see 0x124). Truck 00 00 98 6x Bx 06 75 90; bench module 00 00 FF 60 A2 06 75 90 (first frame after wake 00 00 FE 00 00 06 41 90); bench run 2 b2 FF -> 64 after ~2.3 s. ~1008 ms. Varying bytes [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], typical 00 00 98 68 b6 06 75 90.";
CM_ SG_ 1050 MS_41A_HVAC_Data "[conf=medium] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); bench 0x5xx HVAC+DCSM log 2020-06-12 (bench modules, origin unknown); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF); bench 2020-06-10 (HVAC module alone = NM node 03, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan); bench 2020-06-12 (HVAC node 03 + DCSM node 27, origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan)] Undecoded payload, big-endian integer of all bytes.";
CM_ BO_ 994 "[conf=low] [src=forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus)] Forum 2020 wake set (3E2, 40A, 423, 425, 426, 42C, 10D, 3A0, 3B2, 3B3) = frames 21-30 of the 19:18 KOES truck capture, i.e. one 1-s burst of periodic frames (selected by replaying the first 10/20/30/40/50 frames, inferred). Replayed alone on 2020-06-04 it woke the bench module. Period 1000 ms, varying bytes [0, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], typical 00 00 00 00 00 00 80 4a (key-off log typical 00 00 00 00 00 00 80 4e).";
