CM_ BO_ 1281 "[conf=medium] [src=MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:18 KOES (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus, captures/2020-mscan src22GEX); bench 0x5xx HVAC+DCSM log 2020-06-12 (bench modules, origin unknown); forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834)] Network-management ring, sender node 0x01. Truck ring order 01->03->0B->0C->27->3B->41->01 (successor of this node: 0x03). Ring hop ~200 ms per node. Bench 2020-06-10 20:33 (HVAC alone): 501 03 02 00 at 200 ms -> every reply 503 01 12 00 (Ring to 01 + SleepInd) and HVAC output continuous for the whole 7.5 s log: a stable keep-awake. Tests with the same payload on other IDs failed: 000#030200 (wakes, then 7.4 s wake/sleep cycles), 580#030100 and 583#030100 (LimpHome then sleep after ~5 s). Forum: transmitting 501 03 02 00 every 200 ms keeps the module awake; it replied 503 01 12 00. Bench log: 501 03 02 00 at 200 ms, ring 01->03->27->01.";
CM_ SG_ 1281 DestNode "[conf=high] [src=MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:18 KOES (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus, captures/2020-mscan src22GEX); bench 0x5xx HVAC+DCSM log 2020-06-12 (bench modules, origin unknown); forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834)] b0 = next node in the ring (or own ID in Alive frames).";
