CM_ SG_ 1281 Data_B2 "[conf=low] [src=MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:18 KOES (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus, captures/2020-mscan src22GEX); bench 0x5xx HVAC+DCSM log 2020-06-12 (bench modules, origin unknown); forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834)] Always 00 seen.";
CM_ BO_ 1283 "[conf=medium] [src=MS candump 2020-06-02 19:13/19:16 (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus); MS candump 2020-06-02 19:18 KOES (friend 2011 F-350 truck bus, captures/2020-mscan src22GEX); bench 0x5xx HVAC+DCSM log 2020-06-12 (bench modules, origin unknown); forum 2020 (electro-tech-online 158834); bench wake-set replay 2020-06-04 (bench module(s), origin unknown; captures/2020-mscan src22FF)] Network-management ring, sender node 0x03. Truck ring order 01->03->0B->0C->27->3B->41->01 (successor of this node: 0x0B). Ring hop ~200 ms per node. Bench 2020-06-12: 503 27 12 00 (ring to 0x27) at ~200 ms. Forum reply 01 12 00. Bench 2020-06-10: same pattern after the 7-frame (3E2..10D) and 9-frame (+3B2,3B3) replays; with nonstop 000#030200 traffic it cycles: awake 5.5 s, silent ~1.9 s, wakes again (7.4 s period, HVAC output gone during the gap). Bench replay 2020-06-04, node 03 alone: first 503 within 8-58 ms of the replay (run 2: before 0x3A0 was sent, so 3A0 is not needed to wake it), then 03 01 / 03 02 (Alive / Ring to itself) alternating, LimpHome 03 04 at 1 Hz from +2.46 s, LimpHome+SleepInd 03 14 at +5.48 s, then silence: a one-shot wake burst keeps it up ~5.5 s; staying awake needs an NM ring partner (e.g. 501 03 02 at 200 ms) or continued traffic (inferred).";
